\description{
Selects a sparse model structure by L1 regularisation in the
manner of Hauber, Rosenblatt and Timmer (2023). For every \code{lambda} of the
grid the penalised objective is minimised with \link{trustL1} from several
starts. The structure the best fit lands on (parameters at zero, fused
groups) is then refitted without penalty, and the refits are compared with
the full model.

Three penalties can be combined:
\describe{
\item{\code{zero}}{gates from \link{gateL1}, penalty \code{lambda * s}; a gate at zero
removes its parameter.}
\item{\code{reference}}{parameters pulled toward zero, penalty
\verb{lambda * |r|}, typically log fold changes to a reference cell type.}
\item{\code{groups}}{blocks with the pairwise penalty
\verb{lambda * sum_\{i<j\} |r_i - r_j|}; members with equal values form one
group.}
}
}
\details{
With \code{ssl}, term \code{j} (a gate, a reference parameter, or in a block
the gap between neighbours of the sorted values, anchor included, as in
Ke, Fan and Wu 2015) has the prior
\deqn{\pi(d_j \mid \theta) = \theta\,\psi_1(d_j) + (1-\theta)\,\psi_0(d_j),
  \quad \psi_i(d) = \tfrac{\lambda_i}{4} e^{-\lambda_i |d| / 2},}
so that \verb{-2 log} of each component is \verb{lambda_i * |d|} up to a constant,
the scale of \code{obj}. The posterior mode at one spike strength \code{lambda} is
found by EM: the E-step gives the inclusion probability
\eqn{p_j = \theta\psi_1(d_j) / \pi(d_j \mid \theta)} and
\eqn{\theta = (\sum_j p_j + a - 1)/(J + a + b - 2)}, the M-step is an
L1 fit by \link{trustL1} with weight \eqn{p_j \lambda_1 + (1 - p_j) \lambda}
on term \code{j}, the neighbours taken at the current values. Terms with \eqn{p_j < 1/2} that the weighted fit leaves
off their kink are then put onto it and the EM is rerun; the merge is kept
if it lowers the \verb{-2 log} posterior. The path is one chain over the
increasing grid, each
\code{lambda} started from the optimum of the previous one (Rockova and George
2018) and from the sparse point, then one chain back down; each \code{lambda}
keeps the mode of smaller \verb{-2 log} posterior. \code{pathFits} then only
applies to the refits.
}
\examples{
\dontrun{
## A decays into B, B decays. The model also has a direct loss of A that
## the data do not need; its gate is pulled to exactly zero.
outdir <- tempdir()
f <- eqnvec(A = "-k1 * A - k2 * A", B = "k1 * A - k3 * B")
x <- Xs(odemodel(f, modelname = "scanL1_x", compile = FALSE, outdir = outdir),
        compile = FALSE)
g <- Y(eqnvec(obsA = "A", obsB = "B"), f, modelname = "scanL1_g",
       compile = FALSE, attachInput = FALSE, outdir = outdir)
trafo <- gateL1(eqnvec(A = "1", B = "0", k1 = "10^log10_k1",
                       k2 = "10^log10_k2", k3 = "10^log10_k3"),
                c("k1", "k2", "k3"))
p <- P(trafo, condition = "C1", modelname = "scanL1_p", compile = FALSE,
       outdir = outdir)
compile(g, x, p, output = "scanL1_example")
prd <- g * x * p

set.seed(1)
truth <- c(log10_k1 = log10(0.5), log10_k2 = -1, log10_k3 = log10(0.2),
           s_k1 = 1, s_k2 = 0, s_k3 = 1)
sim <- wide2long(prd(seq(0, 10, 0.5), truth, deriv = FALSE))
sim$value <- sim$value + rnorm(nrow(sim), 0, 0.02)
sim$sigma <- 0.02
obj <- normL2(as.datalist(sim), prd)

fit <- scanL1(obj, c(log10_k1 = 0, log10_k2 = -0.5, log10_k3 = 0),
              zero = attr(trafo, "gates"), lambda = 10^seq(-1, 4, length.out = 11),
              fits = 4)
fit
plot(fit)
plot(fit, type = "test")

## Spike-and-slab lasso: one multistart of the full model, then one chain over
## the spike strength; the structure is the one the chain settles on.
fitS <- scanL1(obj, c(log10_k1 = 0, log10_k2 = -0.5, log10_k3 = 0),
               zero = attr(trafo, "gates"), lambda = 10^seq(0, 4, length.out = 13),
               fits = 4, pathFits = 1, ssl = list(lambda1 = 1), select = "plateau")
fitS
plot(fitS, type = "inclusion")
plot(fitS, type = "waterfall")
}
}
